  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oceans for Development MOZ</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oceans for Development program in Mozambique. The Ocean for Development in Mozambique was launched in 2024, and is set for the program period 2024-2027. This is a bilateral institutional cooperation program between governmental institutions in Norway and Mozambique. The overall goal is to contribute to an &#x201c;enabling environment for sustainable social and economic development, including the importance of increased production and consumption of aquatic foods, contributing to improved food security, nutrition, and livelihoods&#x201d;.

The program is focused around four main areas for cooperation: 1) integrated ocean management; 2), environment &#x2013; marine and coastal, 3) fisheries and aquaculture research and development; and 4) fisheries statistics.

Several Norwegian goverment institutions are involved.</narrative>
  </description>
